diff --git a/Agentic-Practices.md b/Agentic-Practices.md
index a9a0000..126fdd6 100644
--- a/Agentic-Practices.md
+++ b/Agentic-Practices.md
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ pattern lives in this repo, so it can be checked.
 | **Isolated parallel work** | Release fan-outs run one agent per locale and one per ported provider, each restricted to an explicit file list and forbidden the shared files; the orchestrator does shared wiring in one pass afterwards. |
 | **Writer / reviewer** | Three reviewer agents in [`.claude/agents/`](https://github.com/Fighter90/career-ops-ui/tree/main/.claude/agents) — `spa-view-reviewer`, `test-isolation-reviewer`, `web-ui-route-reviewer` — plus an AI review workflow in CI. |
 | **TDD with an agent** | Every ported fix is required to show a **failing run first**. The v1.237.1 Oracle Cloud port opened with `399 !== 453` — the truncation the fix removes. |
-| **Feedback loop the agent can run** | `npm run test:ci` (3776), `npm run test:e2e:browser` (116), `check-changelog-parity`, five registry count gates, and behavioural markers executed against the **deployed** server. |
+| **Feedback loop the agent can run** | `npm run test:ci` (3778), `npm run test:e2e:browser` (116), `check-changelog-parity`, five registry count gates, and behavioural markers executed against the **deployed** server. |
 | **Project memory** | [`CLAUDE.md`](https://github.com/Fighter90/career-ops-ui/blob/main/CLAUDE.md) as a short index (deliberately not a knowledge base — see *Bloated memory* below), `AGENTS.md` for non-Claude CLIs, `.claude/PROJECT-CONTEXT.md` for the per-release record. |
 | **Domain dictionary** | [`CONTEXT.md`](https://github.com/Fighter90/career-ops-ui/blob/main/CONTEXT.md) — one accepted name per concept, variants marked *do not use*. It exists because of a real, recurring confusion: **103 sources vs 98 adapters** (the five RU sources have no adapter), and `telegram` vs `telegram-channel`, which upstream mistook for duplicates and deleted one. |
 | **ADRs** | [`docs/adr/`](https://github.com/Fighter90/career-ops-ui/tree/main/docs/adr) — keep both telegram sources · defend fork divergences · mirror vs relay · liveness hard/soft tiers. |
